orted vocals, distorted speech.","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Jack V","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Music","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16#t=368,608"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Continues \"Poesie Guerriere\", sings [French], music shifts, regular vocals and distorted vocals.","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Jack V","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Music","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16#t=608,703"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Continues \"Poesie Guerriere\", recites poem [French], music shifts, recorded speech and electronic sounds.","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Jack V","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Music","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16#t=703,782"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Bass, electric guitar, drums, and melodic buzzing sound.","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Music","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16#t=782,816"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Continues \"Poesie Guerriere\", recites poem [French] atop electric guitar, drums, and melodic buzzing sound.","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Jack V","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Music","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16#t=816,825"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Electric guitar, drums, bass, melodic buzzing sounds, and kazoo-like sounds.","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Music","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16#t=825,1011"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Keyboard and marching percussion.","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Music","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16#t=1011,1032"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Continues \"Poesie Guerriere\", recites poem atop keyboard and marching percussion.","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Jack V","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Music","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16#t=1032,1075"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Keyboard, marching percussion, and electronic sounds.","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Music","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16#t=1075,1221"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"[End of recording].","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"END","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16#t=1221,1221"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Applause overlaps with music.","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Audience","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Music","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16#t=65,68"}]},{"@context":"http://iiif.io/api/presentation/3/context.json","id":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/manifests/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01-canvas16-1","type":"AnnotationPage","label":{"en":["Alan Lord Commentary"]},"items":[{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"For his performance—called “Poésie guerrière”—Montrealer Jack V starts off by singing while shaving with an electric razor.","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Event Description","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16#t=0,0"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"He says \"sept ans d'malheur!\" (seven years bad luck!) and smashes a mirror","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Event Description","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16#t=61,61"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"The music we hear faintly in the background is the song Hospitality by Sparks","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Event Description","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16#t=89,89"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"He then stripped down to the waist, thus revealing the war paint on his body. He started dancing, prancing and swaying in abandon like a wild man.","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Event Description","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16#t=156,156"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Jack was a member of the Neoists, and played bass in Monty Cantsin’s First Aid Brigade.","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Biographical Context","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16#t=275,275"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Festival participants Jack V, Jean-Luc Bonspiel, Jean-Martin Mignault and I later formed Montreal’s seminal agitrock band Vent du Mont Schärr (1986 – 1990).","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Biographical Context","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16#t=431,431"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"He is joined by a regiment of a half-dozen drummers, one by one—a Post-Punk marching band—martially rat-tatting their snares. Jack was feline and menacing, irresistibly magnetic. This was poetry beyond words, and one of the festival’s highlights.","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Event Description","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Personal Anecdote","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16#t=1008,1008"}]}],"items":[{"id":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01-canvas16/paintings","type":"AnnotationPage","items":[{"id":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01-canvas16/paintings","type":"Annotation","motivation":"painting","body":{"id":"https://youtu.be/4R8HdkNuLHc","type":"Sound","format":"unknown","duration":1221},"target":"https://spokenweb.github.io/Ultimatumi1985/jack_v_at_ultimatum_festival_1985_05_01/canvas/16"}]}]}]}